Ancient Greek philosophy: research completion (@greek-trail-completion: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @greek-scholarly-path) { r_41G7P2Y9HYXMVAF53MV2QYT1CD
The foundation survey and its comparison establish an introductory stage. Full completion of this study requires all of the following evidence:

| Requirement | Demonstration |
| --- | --- |
| Common foundation | The [foundation portfolio](Foundation-readiness.lingua#r_2P555101Z0VGGZ14M12HRWKSYY) covers the major questions and traditions with located primary arguments |
| Working textual command | A [Greek dossier](Philological-study.lingua#r_353E4E4WH3BWFHHJNZMPKBPEXF) defends translation, syntax, relevant editorial decisions, and the passage's context |
| Sustained advanced study | Two [seminar studies](Sustained-study.lingua#r_7WN2AF9HW3X3BNQSTF5CKFJ22Q) address different problem families and include a consequential crossing between texts or traditions |
| Research literature | The [literature dossier](Scholarly-inquiry.lingua#r_2FEBDJ8R5JDHXX54TSATY2CRVZ) represents competing interpretations and situates the proposed contribution |
| Independent investigation | The [research project](Independent-research.lingua#r_08YBJ1G76KSJ3QTG42FKCCAV5K) offers and defends a contribution at an explicit, supported scope |
| Examination and revision | [Informed independent criticism](Criticism-and-revision.lingua#r_5P20QNYEBQPBVGHWV428JXWW8Z) and the resulting revision are documented |
| Final account | The learner identifies the route taken, reused preparation, works and editions studied, demonstrated outcomes, and remaining questions |

Prior work can satisfy a requirement when its evidence meets that requirement's meaning and depth. The same dossier may serve several connected purposes, with the new use explained. A course label, a book count, time spent, or a declaration of completion is not a substitute for the work.

The finish line concerns this authored route and its stated research outcome. Further branches remain available for deeper or different investigations. Its completion claim records the scope actually demonstrated; it does not assert exhaustive knowledge of every ancient Greek text.

Keep the evidence in ordinary notes or Records linked to the studies and sources. The criteria are textual and scholarly requirements; this study introduces no new grading or credential mechanism.

**Home:** [Ancient Greek philosophy](../Ancient-Greek-Philosophy.lingua#r_464ZHR7ZYC234A0XX2QEW47VB3). **Further investigations:** [Seminar families](seminars/Seminars.lingua#r_5FTSQDJTR924S9Z0G9EDBQFR1Y).
